course: dictionary
lesson: 12773
title: An edict is an order
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An edict is an official order or rule. It is usually given by a king, emperor, government or other ruler, and everyone under them must obey it. «The king issued an edict that all roads must be repaired before winter.» The word issued tells you the king gave the order officially, and the rule applies to everyone.
explain: People also use edict as a joke for any strict order from someone in charge. «Mum's edict: no screens until homework is finished.» Mum is not a king, so this is funny: her rule is strict, and nobody is allowed to argue with it.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like issue, royal, ruler and official point to a powerful person making a rule. If you see «by royal edict», royal means belonging to a king or queen, so a royal edict is a rule from a king or queen.
fact: An edict is an official order or rule.
fact: Edicts are usually given by a king, emperor, government or other ruler.
fact: In history, the Edict of Milan in 313 allowed Christians to worship freely in the Roman Empire.
fact: «Issue an edict» means to give out an official order.
fact: Informally, an edict can be any strict order from someone in charge, like a parent or a teacher.
exercise: «The emperor sent out an edict that all bridges must be painted gold.» What is an edict here? | A story about a golden bridge | A kind of boat | *An official order from a ruler | A picture of an emperor
exercise: Mum says, «My edict: no phones at the dinner table.» Why is edict a funny word for her rule? | Mum really is a queen | An edict is always a present | *It is a joke, because a parent's strict rule is called an edict | Edicts are always about food
exercise: Copy the word from «By royal edict, the town gates were closed.» that means an official order. | *edict | town | royal | gates
test:
«The ruler's edict made the market close early.» What does edict mean? | A tasty meal | *An official order from a ruler | A loud noise in the street | A map of the town
Which phrase means to give out an official order? | *issue an edict | eat a biscuit | draw a picture | climb a tree
exam:
«Sam's dad made a strict edict: bedtime is at eight, no arguing.» In this sentence, edict means | A kind of bed | A type of food | *A strict order from someone in charge | A sleepy noise
